<PageTitle>TV Promotions</PageTitle>

<section class="page-section narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">TV Promotions</p>
    <h1>Promote your station with Tracking The Eye.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The original TV promotions page offered custom station-branded versions of Tracking The Eye so broadcasters could drive more visitors to their websites while giving viewers a useful hurricane tool.</p>
</section>

<section class="muted-panel wide">
    <p><strong>"We would like you to promote your station with our software by putting your station's logo on our software and we guarantee it will bring visitors to your web site that had never been there before."</strong></p>
    <p>Tracking The Eye was pitched as a professional and easy to use application that stations could offer as their own promotional device. Your station would send the logo, and a custom version of the software could then help viewers return to your website throughout hurricane season.</p>
    <p>Stations called out on the original page included Univision Puerto Rico, Fox News, KVUE Austin, WPLG Miami, WWBT Richmond, WCPX Orlando, WPEC TV12, KWCH Wichita, and KHOU Houston.</p>
    <h2>How the station was promoted</h2>
    <ul class="detail-list">
        <li>Opening splash screen.</li>
        <li>Your logo on top of the map on screen.</li>
        <li>Your logo on top of the map on printouts.</li>
        <li>Your logo on the button bar.</li>
        <li>Custom station message when the button bar is pressed.</li>
        <li>Daily station messaging when users connect for coordinates.</li>
        <li>Optional local radar links in place of standard satellite imagery.</li>
        <li>Technical support and a package of free registrations for local schools.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you need more information on the archived TV promotion program, use the contact page and mention TV Promotions.</p>
</section>
